course: dictionary
lesson: 4884
title: Idol: a hero, a statue, or too much love
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so use the context clues to choose the right one. Ask who or what is being talked about, and what the words around it suggest. «My childhood idol» and the TV phrase «pop idols» mean a person who is greatly admired and loved.
explain: In religion, an idol is a statue or picture that people worship as a god. The sentence «The commandment against idols forbids making carved images to worship» uses the clues «carved images» and «worship» to show this meaning.
explain: The third meaning is something treated as more important than it should be. In «Money became his idol», the word money tells you the man cares for money above everything else. Test your meaning in the sentence: "Money became the thing he worshipped" fits well, so the meaning is right.
fact: «Idol» is a noun. One idol, or more than one: idols.
fact: «Idol» can mean a person who is greatly admired and loved, such as a pop star or sports star.
fact: «Idol» can mean a statue or picture that is worshipped as a god, and the Bible forbids worshipping idols.
fact: «Idol» can mean anything treated as more important than it should be, as in «Money became his idol».
fact: «Moorish idol» is also the name of a reef fish, as in «the Moorish idol, is one of the hardest to keep alive».
exercise: «Many reef fish in the film are hard to keep in tanks. Gill's kind, the Moorish idol, is one of the hardest to keep alive.» What is a Moorish idol? | A statue in a temple | *A kind of reef fish | A pop star who sings on TV | A tank for keeping fish
exercise: «The commandment against idols forbids making carved images to worship.» What is an idol in this sentence? | A footballer everybody cheers | A kind of salt water | *A carved statue or picture worshipped as a god | A word for money
exercise: «Money became his idol.» What does this mean? | He is sad that he has no money | *He treats money as more important than it should be | He admires money the way a famous pop star is admired | He buys a golden statue
test: «She wanted to be like her childhood idol, a famous singer.» What does idol mean here? | A carved statue in a temple | *A person who is greatly admired and loved | A fish in a tank | Something treated as too important
test: «Orthodox and Catholics use icons and statues to help prayer, while some Protestants avoid them, so this point is disputed.» What does disputed mean? | Agreed by everyone | A kind of statue | It is very old | *People argue about it and do not agree
exam: What does «idol» mean in «The Bible forbids worshipping idols»? | Something you love too much | *A statue or picture worshipped as a god | A pop star who sings on TV | A reef fish
